// The carrier keeps keyed (object = map) and indexed (array = vector)
// members in SEPARATE kinds — madarray_key_slot / madarray_index_slot
// each vivify their own kind and refuse the other at runtime. A literal
// mixing a string key with a positional (or integer-keyed) element can
// never construct, so it refuses at COMPILE time with the kinds named.
int main()
{
	var bad = { 7, "k": "v" };
	return 0;
}
